Source: media-gpu-route
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 14), cmake, pkgconf, libvulkan-dev, libdrm-dev, libva-dev, libffmpeg-nvenc-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.3
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libmedia-gpu-route0
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: shared display GPU preference for media engines
 Resolves the graphics driver's default hardware GPU, including the
 compositor's display preference and explicit driver overrides.
 Decoder selection checks codec, component depth and chroma capabilities
 before startup and retains software fallback. Hardware decoding that
 copies every picture back is chosen only where the person or the
 machine's measured record allows it.
 It writes no user settings.

Package: libmedia-gpu-route-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libmedia-gpu-route0 (= ${binary:Version}), libavcodec-dev, libavutil-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: development files for shared media GPU routing
 Headers and linker metadata for media-gpu-route.

Package: media-gpu-route-tools
Section: utils
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: libmedia-gpu-route0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: inspect the default display GPU for media engines
 Prints the selected hardware device and its DRM render node, each GPU's
 zero-copy import capability, the copy-back choice and the decoder chosen
 for a source, for isolated qualification and diagnosis.
